Subject: [PATCH 04/69] fix: bump freenet-stdlib to 0.1.40 to fix ErrorKind
 deserialization crash (#115)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* fix: bump freenet-stdlib to 0.1.40 to fix ErrorKind deserialization crash

Closes #114. The deployed UI WASM was compiled against freenet-stdlib
0.1.35, which only knows 12 ErrorKind variants (indices 0-11). When the
node (running stdlib >= 0.1.38) sends EmptyRing (index 12) or
PeerNotJoined (index 13), bincode deserialization fails with:
  "invalid value: integer 12, expected variant index 0 <= i < 12"

- Bump freenet-stdlib from 0.1.35 to 0.1.40 in workspace and CLI
- Handle new InboundDelegateMsg variants in chat-delegate
- Add regression test asserting the new ErrorKind variants exist

* test: add bincode round-trip tests for ErrorKind deserialization

Add bincode as a dev-dependency and test that EmptyRing and
PeerNotJoined variants survive serialize/deserialize — the exact
path that crashed in the browser WebSocket handler.
